  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Myanmar refugees in Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Border Consortium (TBC), formally known as the Thai Burma Border Consortium (TBBC), is the largest of several organisations supporting Myanmar refugees living in camps along the Thai-Myanmar border.  Support includes provision of food rations, housing materials and other basic essentials (soap, clothing etc), and the coordination of camp management committees. TBC has introduced agriculture and income generation projects to their programme to enable the refugees to maintain and develop their skills whilst earning minimal additional income. TBC supports camp management costs and capacity building, providing training to refugee camp committees and CBOs, to allow for effective running of the 9 camps. TBC also engages in research on the root causes of displacement and refugee outflows, regularly producing reports which are used for advocacy and information flow.  Programmes are implemented in the field through refugees, community based organisations and local partners, and every effort is made to involve the refugees themselves in designing, implementing and monitoring activities.  TBC is mandated by the Royal Thai Government and has registered charity status in England and Wales.  As an active (and founding) member of the Committee for Co-ordination of Services to Displaced Persons in Thailand (CCSDPT), TBC is fully authorised to work in the refugee camps, and has signed up to a commonly agreed inter-agency Code of Conduct intended to prevent, or respond appropriately to, any possibility of abuse or exploitation.  This Code of Conduct has been developed in the spirit of complementing and strengthening similar Codes or other instruments within each agency. TBC have recently established an office in Yangon in order to explore opportunities for engagement with the Myanmar government and begin more substantial cross-border activities.</narrative>
  </description>
